  "id": "COMPOUND:15910 - PROTEIN:5677",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 9-Angeloylretronecine and JM1 through a series of target-mediated pathways. The drug 9-Angeloylretronecine is implicated in targeting Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including 2-Methoxyjuglone, Dihydrostreptomycin Sulfate, and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. All of these compounds ultimately target JM1, indicating a possible downstream effect of 9-Angeloylretronecine on JM1 through the activation of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. The evidence suggests that 9-Angeloylretronecine may act as a modulator of the activity of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which in turn influences JM1 through its downstream targets. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which 9-Angeloylretronecine could interact with JM1, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
